{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMpxQHNPxDmg1rznBqLF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XDXnTkhHHH28P7uJWcKULD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='docs/layout.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nl=\"internal/botcheck/          tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\\n\"\ns=s.replace(l,l+\"internal/versioncheck/       tests for the version workflow in .github/workflows/version.yml (plan and tag scripts)\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- **Release.** An annotated tag\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"- **Versioning ([#183](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/183)).** `version.yml` gives every first-parent merge to `main` an annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` and a notes-only release, oldest first. The bump comes from the merged PR's labels: `semver:major`, `semver:minor`, else patch; a direct push gets patch, and ard's own main-lane commits (committer `ARD_BOT_LOGIN`) are skipped. The seed tag is `v0.1.0`. The workflow is a dry run until the repository variable `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. `make build` (`git describe` limited to plain `vX.Y.Z` tags) and `go install ...@vX.Y.Z` (build info) both print the tag from `ard version`. `internal/versioncheck` tests the workflow's scripts. See `docs/runbooks/release.md`.\\n\"+a,1)\ns=s.replace(\"Releases do not change what is deployed, which follows `main`.\",\"Every merge to `main` is tagged by the Versioning step above; releases do not change what is deployed, which follows `main`.\",1)\ng=\"- **Merges are gated.**\"\ns=s.replace(g,\"- **The tag-writing credential is separate.** Only the `tag` job of `version.yml`, in the `release` environment, holds a token that can push tags, from a release App that must differ from ard's App (the job refuses otherwise). Tags are never moved or deleted. The logic is inline bash under `.github/`, which agents cannot change, and `internal/versioncheck` tests it.\\n\"+g,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nmkdir -p docs/runbooks; cat > docs/runbooks/release.md <<'E'\n# Release runbook\n\n`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## Seed tag\n\nAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\ngit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n```\n\nUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n\n## Settings checklist\n\n- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n\n## Dry run to live\n\nEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n\n## Bumps and the module path\n\nLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n\n## Recovery\n\n- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8826,"cache_read_input_tokens":32284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8826},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25ca8ac6-8c6f-4027-a2a7-ce1fe421e1d1","uuid":"460e592a-09b2-454e-8766-d288d15b6d64","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:25:15.974Z","request_id":"req_011ChMpxQ6CjqW47pMDywoSW"}
